# Shared by every docker/Dockerfile.* — each builds with the repo ROOT as its
# context, so patterns below are relative to it. Do not add a per-Dockerfile
# docker/Dockerfile.<variant>.dockerignore: BuildKit uses that file INSTEAD of
# this one, so every exclusion here would silently stop applying to that image.
#
# The Dockerfiles use explicit COPYs (never `COPY . .`), so most entries here
# only keep the context sent to the daemon small/fast — especially the multi-GB
# weights/ and data/. The first group is different: those files sit INSIDE a
# copied dir, so this file is the only thing keeping them out of the image.

# Gitignored machine-local settings (e.g. the real bucket URI). The published
# images are public, so these must never be baked in.
configs/jobs/local.env
**/.env
**/.envrc

# Large / runtime-populated dirs (gitignored) — mounted or synced at run time.
weights/
data/
outputs/
logs/

# Not needed in the image.
jobs/
demos/
docs/
venvs/

# VCS / tooling / caches.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Test scratch (tests/ itself IS copied for `pytest --quick`).
tests/_tmp/

# Editor / OS cruft.
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
